---
title: "I started sending the screenshot first"
description: "Talking about AI got me polite nods. Showing the before and after got me yeses."
date: "2026-07-18"
tags:
  - growth
  - saas
published: true
layout: docs
---

I used to open calls with a story about what we could build. People nodded. Then they ghosted.

Now I send a screenshot or a short loom of the actual workflow before we even meet. Broken state. Fixed state. What changed. It's less impressive as a speech and way more useful as a decision.

If I can't show it, I'm not ready to sell it. That rule has saved me from a lot of vague conversations that were never going to close.
